{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall lean his hand upon the head of the burnt offering.</b> It is known that the leaning is with both hands, for so they interpreted in Torat Kohanim (ibid.): ״And Aaron shall lean both his hands״ — this teaches that the leaning is with both hands, and this is a paradigm for all leaning, that it be with both hands, end quote. But the fact that <b>his hand</b> is written here in the singular comes to exclude the agent, for even though in every matter a person's agent is like him, this was not said regarding leaning, and therefore ״his hand״ is written in the singular. And the leaning was only in the Temple courtyard, and immediately after the leaning comes the slaughter, and he must lean with all his strength with both his hands upon the head of the animal, as it is written ״upon the head of the burnt offering״ — not upon the neck and not upon the sides."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:22:28.547090749Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}